The contract also holds for the inputs the step regexes admit beyond this scenario: `^the number is (\d+)$` permits any non-negative integer literal, and `Double(0) == 0`, `Double(7) == 14`, and so on all follow from sum-with-itself. No special-casing of 3 or 6, and no lookup table — a hard-coded result for the scenario's literals would satisfy this one test while violating the stated term, and must not be used.

